Name: startListening

Type: command

Syntax: startListening [<language>]

Summary:
Starts the speech recognition engine. Once listening, the engine matches
spoken audio against registered voice command phrases and dispatches
<voiceCommand> messages when a match is found.

Introduced: 1.1.0

OS: mac

Platforms: desktop

Example:
-- Start listening using the system locale
startListening

Example:
-- Start listening in a specific language
startListening "fr-FR"

Example:
-- Typical setup sequence
registerVoiceCommand "next slide"
registerVoiceCommand "previous slide"
startListening "en-US"
if the result is not empty then
    answer "Could not start listening: " & the result
end if

Parameters:
language (string): An optional BCP-47 language tag that sets the
recognition locale (e.g. "en-US", "fr-FR", "de-DE", "ja-JP"). If
omitted or empty, the system default locale is used.

Description:
Call <startListening> after registering the phrases you want to recognise
with <registerVoiceCommand>. The engine runs continuously in the background
until <stopListening> is called.

On first use, macOS will prompt the user to grant microphone access and
speech recognition permission. If either permission is denied,
<startListening> sets the result to a human-readable error string and
returns false. Check the result after calling <startListening> in
production code.

Calling <startListening> when the engine is already running is a no-op
and succeeds silently. The language parameter is ignored on subsequent
calls; call <stopListening> first if you need to change the locale.

Platform notes:
- macOS: Uses SFSpeechRecognizer (macOS 10.15+) with AVAudioEngine.
  On macOS 13+, on-device recognition is used (no internet required).
  The NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription and NSMicrophoneUsageDescription
  keys must be present in the application's Info.plist.
- Windows: Not yet implemented. Sets the result to a "not supported"
  error string and returns without starting.
- Linux: Not yet implemented. Sets the result to a "not supported"
  error string and returns without starting.

References: stopListening (command), registerVoiceCommand (command),
setWakeWord (command), isListening (function), voiceCommand (message)

Tags: speech, voice
